  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/fc474c9e41e73e04b3e4312e285726b9095a59f598016f6421943e0604d23abe.png)\n\nLet $U={1,2,3,a,b,c,d}$ be the universal set and let $W={3,b,c}.$ What is $\\overset{\u2015}{W}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $W,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{W},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $W.$ To represent $\\overset{\u2015}{W},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $W,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/365a6446a4ec6993447cf11190c8311027fac5bc9b0b36e85a4452fdfe85f7fa.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $1,2,a,$ and $d.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $W.$ Therefore, the complement of $W$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{W}={1,2,a,d}.\n$$",
